FiKTZjHOu2tj28ZczEzOBnSLdz9Q&oe=699B0256"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": {"file_name": "Laboratory Safety Training_Landscape.png", "id": "670218148403280", "uri": "https://scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/38974920_670218155069946_1643766435637563529_n.png?_nc_cat=100&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=CQdnu8WN-4UQ7kNvwEVs3mL&_nc_oc=AdmE3X7jnsqSU6XEEht3LUSuems9nrYcMxuqENJeOj6MxAmIOpkDRfiAwcJF1wJzaK4&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-ord5-3.oculuscdn.com&oh=00_AftfJcAY28Li8Lq_nUkqyA2qfrj_ZGqlnNGhyttqmwIxHQ&oe=699B0FDC"}, "display_name": "Laboratory Safety Training- ContentsDa", "keywords": ["safety", "laboratory", "accident", "simulation", "contentsda"], "long_description": "1. Prepare for lab safety incidents: Put on safety equipment before your experiment. Wear safety glasses and a lab coat.\n2. How to operate an alkaline lamp: Find the alkaline lamp and igniter, place it on the white table, and flick the flame to experience fire.\n3. burn treatment: soak the burned area in water to reduce the heat and wrap it with clean gauze.\n4. Staunching wounds: Use clean gauze to staunch bleeding if a tool breaks during the experiment.\n5. organize experimental tools: put the alcohol lamp in the display case after the experiment is finished.\n6. fire response: If a fire occurs, use the fire extinguisher near the door to extinguish the fire.", "short_description": "Master the essential safety protocols for working in a laboratory. This training covers proper handling of chemicals, equipment use, and emergency procedures, ensuring a safe and informed lab environment."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/privacy-policy-en/", "developer_terms_of_service_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/terms-and-conditions-en/", "publisher_name": "ContentsDa Inc", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://training.contentsda.kr/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "NOT_RATED", "comfort_tags": [], "context